WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:06.019
It's almost a new year, and as it does every
month, Netflix is celebrating impending newness

00:00:06.019 --> 00:00:08.109
with a slew of fresh releases.

00:00:08.109 --> 00:00:12.790
From new hits to classic Scorsese mob films,
here are the releases you definitely won't

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:15.620
want to miss on Netflix in January 2021.

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:20.810
If you're someone who can't get enough of
Netflix's original movies, you'll be delighted

00:00:20.810 --> 00:00:26.179
to hear that the streamer has a solid selection
of new projects set to kick off 2021.

00:00:26.179 --> 00:00:30.170
Fans of fairy tales looking for a new take
on an old classic will definitely want to

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:34.989
check out Charming, an irreverent animated
flick that forces Prince Charming to seek

00:00:34.989 --> 00:00:40.160
out his one true love, rather than the other
way around; the film drops on January 8.

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:45.210
Then, on January 15, you'll want to catch
Outside the Wire, which features Marvel Cinematic

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:50.570
Universe favorite Anthony Mackie and Damson
Idris as a droid officer and drone pilot that

00:00:50.570 --> 00:00:52.500
team up in a futuristic military zone.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:53.600
"We remove advanced weapons from beyond the
wire."

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:56.640
Together, the two must find a doomsday device
before it's too late.

00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:02.590
On January 27, don't miss Penguin Bloom, which
stars Naomi Watts, Andrew Lincoln, and Jacki

00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:05.580
Weaver as a family struck by tragedy.

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:08.600
Their lives are turned around by a tiny injured
bird named Penguin.

00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:15.510
After buzzy December 2020 debuts like Shonda
Rhimes' period piece Bridgerton and new seasons

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:20.050
of Big Mouth and Chilling Adventures of Sabrina,
there aren't quite as many new shows dropping

00:01:20.050 --> 00:01:21.150
in the new year.

00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:25.790
However, the exciting news is that some beloved
favorites are returning for new installments.

00:01:25.790 --> 00:01:30.460
At the top of the month, Netflix subscribers
can see Nicolas Cage share the interesting

00:01:30.460 --> 00:01:35.780
and unexpected origins of the English language's
most... colorful words in History of Swear

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:39.080
Words, which arrives on the platform on January
5.

00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:44.460
A bit later, Disenchantment fans can finally
see Part 3 of the medieval-fantasy-kingdom-set

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:45.810
animated series.

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:52.200
On January 21, the French comedy Call My Agent!,
which features Emily in Paris star Philippine

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:54.610
Leroy-Beaulieu, returns for its fourth season.

00:01:54.610 --> 00:01:58.531
If you haven't checked out the sharp show-business
comedy, now's the time.

00:01:58.531 --> 00:02:02.520
Though there's no release date just yet for
the highly anticipated third season of Cobra

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:07.521
Kai, the modern spin-off of the Karate Kid
story, fans can get excited: The new season

00:02:07.521 --> 00:02:09.340
will hit the service sometime in January.

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:13.570
"Put one of those hashbrowns at the end, you
know like 'hashbrown team Cobra Kai' or something.

00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:16.381
And then send it to the internet!"

00:02:17.381 --> 00:02:21.890
If you want to revisit some classics and favorites
in January 2021, Netflix definitely has you

00:02:21.890 --> 00:02:22.890
covered.

00:02:22.890 --> 00:02:26.830
A huge group of movies hits the service on
New Year's Day, so you can start your year

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:32.170
off right on January 1 with everything from
Academy-Award-nominated flicks to gut-busting

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:33.170
comedies.

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:34.170
"Fo sho.

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:35.170
Fo sho.

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:36.850
I'm gettin' that fo sho."

00:02:36.850 --> 00:02:41.630
A small selection of the January 1 drop includes
favorites like Steven Spielberg's Catch Me

00:02:41.630 --> 00:02:47.990
If You Can, Martin Scorsese's Goodfellas and
The Departed, the feel-good biopic Julie &amp; Julia,

00:02:47.990 --> 00:02:53.040
Julia Roberts' beloved romantic comedy Mystic
Pizza, the first Robert Downey Jr.-led Sherlock

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:58.400
Holmes movie, both Sex and the City films,
and the raucous coming-of-age comedy Superbad

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:00.240
– to name just a few.

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:04.070
After that, a few more awesome movies will
join the Netflix ranks — including The Girl

00:03:04.070 --> 00:03:09.180
with the Dragon Tattoo, Spring Breakers, and
Hook, which hit the service on January 5,

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:12.330
January 10, and January 15, respectively.

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:17.620
As Netflix subscribers continue to hunker
down at home in January 2021, they certainly

00:03:17.620 --> 00:03:20.670
won't be hurting for options whenever they
want a movie night.

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:26.340
Netflix is adding a handful of new and returning
non-original shows to the service in January

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:29.260
2021, but there's one big standout.

00:03:29.260 --> 00:03:34.750
On January 15, the fifth and final season
of the buzzy Syfy series The Magicians – which,

00:03:34.750 --> 00:03:39.130
with its focus on teenagers at a secret school
of magic, is sort of like a darker take on

00:03:39.130 --> 00:03:40.850
Harry Potter — arrives on Netflix.

00:03:40.850 --> 00:03:43.730
"Are we in trouble again?"

00:03:43.730 --> 00:03:44.730
"Duh."

00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:48.900
Pretty soon, fans of The Magicians will be
able to catch the latest season of their favorite

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:49.900
show.

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:55.040
If you're looking for hard-hitting documentaries
on Netflix in January 2021, the service has

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:56.040
you covered.

00:03:56.040 --> 00:04:00.490
On January 1, learn how to make your everyday
life more efficient with The Minimalists:

00:04:00.490 --> 00:04:01.490
Less Is Now.

00:04:01.490 --> 00:04:07.160
A few days later, on January 6, you can check
out Surviving Death, a series about the possibility

00:04:07.160 --> 00:04:12.010
of an afterlife, as well as Tony Parker: The
Final Shot, a look at the life and games of

00:04:12.010 --> 00:04:14.470
French basketball star Tony Parker.

00:04:14.470 --> 00:04:19.690
Pretend It's a City, writer Fran Lebowitz's
wry take on Manhattan, arrives on the service

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:20.940
on January 8.

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:25.340
"Now, everybody is looking at the phone, and
they've bequeathed the entire city to me.

00:04:25.340 --> 00:04:26.930
They're basically saying, 'Fran, it's all
yours.

00:04:26.930 --> 00:04:27.930
You know this.'"

00:04:27.930 --> 00:04:32.220
On January 11, you can learn more about the
history of one of America's most infamous

00:04:32.220 --> 00:04:36.210
illegal drugs in CRACK: Cocaine, Corruption,
&amp; Conspiracy.

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:42.050
Two days after that doc's arrival on Netflix,
travel back to 1985 and learn about a real-life

00:04:42.050 --> 00:04:45.220
manhunt in Night Stalker: The Hunt for a Serial
Killer.

00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:49.910
Finally, on January 29, follow the Brooklyn
Saints football players and their crusade

00:04:49.910 --> 00:04:54.290
to make the world a better place in the four-part
series We Are: The Brooklyn Saints.

00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:59.640
As is the norm on Netflix, in order to make
room for all the stellar new films and shows

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:04.389
arriving to the digital library during any
given month, the streamer must do away with

00:05:04.389 --> 00:05:09.240
a number of other flicks and series — even
ones that subscribers hold near and dear.

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:14.880
January 2021 marks the last chance for Netflix
subscribers to stream dozens of great titles

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:19.450
— including four seasons of The Tudors,
which leave on January 7.

00:05:19.450 --> 00:05:25.050
2018's Mary Poppins Returns flies away from
Netflix via a magical umbrella on January

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:26.050
8.

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:30.600
The critically acclaimed drama Dallas Buyers
Club exits the streaming platform on January

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:31.600
15.

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:37.300
And the Daniel Radcliffe-starring black-comedy-drama
Swiss Army Man swims away on January 29.

00:05:37.300 --> 00:05:42.290
A little before then, those who like to turn
to Netflix and use their laptops or TV screens

00:05:42.290 --> 00:05:47.639
as a digital fireplace will be sad to hear
that a bundle of fake fireplace streams – Fireplace

00:05:47.639 --> 00:05:53.710
4K: Classic Crackling Fireplace from Fireplace
for Your Home, Fireplace 4K: Crackling Birchwood

00:05:53.710 --> 00:05:58.360
from Fireplace for Your Home, and Fireplace
for Your Home — will be gone from Netflix

00:05:58.360 --> 00:06:00.310
on January 20.

00:06:00.310 --> 00:06:04.610
Before the end of the month, be sure to load
up Death at a Funeral, Employee of the Month,

00:06:04.610 --> 00:06:09.440
For Colored Girls, Mr. Deeds, and Pineapple
Express, as they're all leaving Netflix on

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:10.530
January 31, 2021.

00:06:10.530 --> 00:06:15.740
"Think about a hermit crab, okay, and it's
a shell, it's like they go from one shell

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:18.930
to the next.

00:06:18.930 --> 00:06:23.270
And that's what I am, it's like, I'm just
a hermit crab changing shells."

00:06:23.270 --> 00:06:25.419
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:06:25.419 --> 00:06:29.720
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
stuff are coming soon.

00:06:29.720 --> 00:06:32.999
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

